[3.211186, "o", "1/3  Prove the configured Chrome ClientHello matches its expected JA4\r\n"]
[3.334055, "o", "target:       modern-origin:8443\r\nprofile:      chrome-152-linux\r\nexpected JA4: t13d1517h2_8daaf6152771_cb7bf5808d99\r\nobserved JA4: t13d1517h2_8daaf6152771_cb7bf5808d99\r\nresult:       PASS\r\nattempt 1:    profile; captured=2037 bytes; tls=TLS1.3; cipher=TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256; alpn=http/1.1\r\n"]
[3.350223, "o", "\r\n2/3  Send plaintext HTTP through Mimic and inspect its HTTP identity\r\n"]
[3.358722, "o", "{\r\n  \"protocol\": \"HTTP/1.1\",\r\n  \"tls\": \"none\",\r\n  \"user_agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/152.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\"\r\n}\r\n\r\n3/3  Let Mimic intercept HTTPS and originate the upstream TLS connection\r\n"]
[3.370252, "o", "{\r\n  \"protocol\": \"HTTP/1.1\",\r\n  \"tls\": \"TLS1.3\",\r\n  \"cipher\": \"TLS_AES_128_GCM_SHA256\",\r\n  \"user_agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/152.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\"\r\n}\r\n\r\nSuccess: JA4 conformance, profiled HTTP, and HTTPS interception worked.\r\n"]
